{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic","id":834254,"title":"Changeling the lost demographic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-20T21:41:48-08:00","id":834254,"title":"Changeling the lost demographic","content":"I believe this is left deliberately ambiguous in the CofD books and i know that it may vary from game to game, but i really want to know.<br /> <br /> What do you think is a good number of changelings to mortals ratio in a city? <br /> <br /> What problems could arise with a really large changeling population or what could limit their numbers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T21:52:57-08:00","id":834259,"title":"","content":"I would make the Freehold first. Figure out how many Lost are needed to fill out your Court titles, maintain your Bulwark, plus some extra to round out the hold. (This still works if you're using 1e, just fill out the titles for the seasonal courts and add a few extra). That's how many Lost are in your city. From there you can check census information to find out how many people there are and it's just some division to figure out the ratio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T22:02:07-08:00","id":834265,"title":"","content":"I think this has to do in part with what you and your players are into, as well as what the game needs. I'm a pretty political guy and like dealing with large group dynamics; the kind of populations people often posit seem incredibly small and restrained to me, an artificial social horizon just as forced as the hero of the story always needing to deal with friends and rivals instead of institutions or the needs of the many. So I tend to bulk numbers up for games like Vampire or (often) Changeling, where I want to see parties and factions and so forth. For a game like Mage, the size of a university's faculty community is a feature. For Werewolf, numbers often detract. So: think about what purpose groups serve in your game, how numbers work with the game's themes, and what kind of social canvas your players are into.<br /> <br /> I often think of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunbar%27s_number\" target=\"_blank\">Dunbar's Number</a> as a handy dividing line; if you're keeping it below 100-150, everybody in the community is going to know each other somewhat personally. Start going above that number and you're talking groups instead of people. Most WoD games steer towards below that number, because it's easier for people to keep straight in their head, less work for the ST, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T22:59:20-08:00","id":834281,"title":"","content":"Half year ago we have the discussion about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city\">supernatural populations numbers based on the <b>Beast: The Primodrial</b> SAS <i>&quot;Morning After&quot;</i> estimations</a>. Here is the most accurate sum up we come with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city?p=590845#post590845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least if we don't assume even more splats, those seem as pretty good numbers. As a rule of thumb, so, we can agree that a regular city will have 0,05% of its population as Major Monsters. That is, 1:2.000 people. Any given splat that forms a comunity will be little more than 1:20.000. I personaly would like even less, but can't complain about it now. Among other things, I don't see the need to account every splat for every urban area. Any city can be free of some of those guys.<br /> <br /> From them, we have how to figure variations. Those numbers should work best on big cities and metropolitan areas. Big places, with enough people, variability and travel routes to effectively run toward middle numbers.<br /> <br /> The smaller the place, the more it can change from the expected numbers. The thing here isn't to avoid this, but to account for consequences. A community with more of any given splat than it should support will be more affected for it. Well, the kind of stories told by the WoD does have as a common trope the Secrets of the Small Towns.<br /> <br /> So when dealing with a less populated region, decide cautiously about the numbers. Mantaining those numbers or even reducing them should make for a game of few splats. That isn't bad. With few vamps, wolfs, mages or fae you would have a game with themes of isolation, strangeness, or even pioneering, as well as possible incestuous societies, where you have to deal constantly with the same faces every time. Such a theme can make great games.<br /> <br /> Making for more splats on such places isn't bad, either. The thing here is to remember that you just broke the security line. Your chosen splat will have a greater impact, more people will know and this society will be even culturally affected by this situations. Imagine a town where everyone knows that you shouldn't cross the path of the people of the Hill. Or a city where the Mayor is chosen by unknown hands, and he and his officers learn of the true powers that be.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want this, most people want moar numbah without it being really necessary. Some chronicles won't need more than 40 vampires living in the city at a time, never, not even accounting for the nameless guys to give the impression of a full party. You can give the impression of a complex All Night Society with just that much. And if you ever need a new guy, remember that you can bring him into the fold from the outside. The PCs aren't the only new Embraces, specially when people die. And remember those outcities numbers. Travelers can easily account for new characters when you need them and left quick enough for you to not have to bother with the numbers.<br /> <br /> By my side, I would use 1:25 instead of 1:10, but again, personal taste. With that I can move more freely the numbers and cut out some splats to give room to the ones I think should live there. I don't see most cities housing every splat, or even every social splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>General numbers are 1:20 000 Major Template to mortals ration. You can make those number fluctuate to the needs of your setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:15:38-08:00","id":834285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834281#post834281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General numbers are 1:20 000 Major Template to mortals ration. You can make those number fluctuate to the needs of your setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that'd put only 16 changelings for the region my group was going to be in and that region is the third most populated in the state (and since it's australia states are not small).... Can't believe someone would want even less than 1:20 000 considering how small that makes supernatural populations.<br /> <br /> edit: Wait... No 16 Major template supernaturals..... Well there goes werewolves and changelings....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-21-2016, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:52:26-08:00","id":834296,"title":"","content":"The answer is &quot;However many you need for your game.&quot; For me, since I tend towards large city settings, I often get away with centering my numbers around 300 per gameline and still come nowhere near a noticeable population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T00:25:52-08:00","id":834306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834285#post834285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that'd put only 16 changelings for the region my group was going to be in and that region is the third most populated in the state (and since it's australia states are not small).... Can't believe someone would want even less than 1:20 000 considering how small that makes supernatural populations.<br /> <br /> edit: Wait... No 16 Major template supernaturals..... Well there goes werewolves and changelings....</div> </div> </div> </div>They are &quot;examinations&quot; - I run game in small town in New England of 2000 mortal with 10 changelings in there. It just implying there<i><b> are weird things going there</b></i> with this numbers - and chronicle setting was a bit much cooler that way when players try to understand &quot;WHY SO MANY&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And remember what I qouted in respons of <b>monteparnas</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>The smaller the place, the more it can change from the expected numbers. The thing here isn't to avoid this, but to account for consequences. A community with more of any given splat than it should support will be more affected for it. Well, the kind of stories told by the WoD does have as a common trope the Secrets of the Small Towns.</i><br /> <br /> <i>So when dealing with a less populated region, decide cautiously about the numbers. Mantaining those numbers or even reducing them should make for a game of few splats. That isn't bad. With few vamps, wolfs, mages or fae you would have a game with themes of isolation, strangeness, or even pioneering, as well as possible incestuous societies, where you have to deal constantly with the same faces every time. Such a theme can make great games.</i><br /> <br /> I have also running now game with 4 Awakening mortals in 1000 population town, so this is okay for me still. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i>Stephen's King</i> weirdness of small towns in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> universe kinda bound to slightly higher supernatural numbers &quot;in the woods&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-21-2016, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T00:39:04-08:00","id":834308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834306#post834306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The smaller the place, the more it can change from the expected numbers. The thing here isn't to avoid this, but to account for consequences. A community with more of any given splat than it should support will be more affected for it. Well, the kind of stories told by the WoD does have as a common trope the Secrets of the Small Towns.</i><br /> <br /> <i>So when dealing with a less populated region, decide cautiously about the numbers. Mantaining those numbers or even reducing them should make for a game of few splats. That isn't bad. With few vamps, wolfs, mages or fae you would have a game with themes of isolation, strangeness, or even pioneering, as well as possible incestuous societies, where you have to deal constantly with the same faces every time. Such a theme can make great games.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That didn't really apply to what I was talking about though since... well it's not a small place, it's one of the most populated regions in the most populated state of a continent. My issue with 1:20,000 is that it only seems to make any sense with the biggest of the biggest cities on the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:10:29-08:00","id":834373,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks for all the answers so far. A few extra things to consider. Firstly my groups worlds of darkness differ particualry from the standard game in that there are no other splats in the games. For all intents and purposes, tehre are onyl mortals, changelings and their antagonists in a city. That i believe can extend the number of since changelings are relatively harmless to humans. Yes there would be a lot of abductions but fetches take care of many of those and not all changelings coming back most have being taken from the same city. And depresion or stress could be a reasonable explanation for few thousand reticent mortals in a city<br /> <br /> And for the purposes of this topic a want to go large. whats stopping me from having a 1:1000 ratio of changelings in a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:25:15-08:00","id":834381,"title":"","content":"My eyebally rule of thumb is to have a number of tiers:<br /> <br /> Tier 0: Limited number in existence (Mummy).<br /> Tier 1: One per hundred million (Promethean).<br /> Tier 2: One per hundred thousand (Sin-Eater, Demon?, Beast?).<br /> Tier 3: One per ten thousand (Changeling, Mage).<br /> Tier 4: One per five thousand (Vampire, Werewolf).<br /> Tier 5: One per thousand (Hunter, Minor Template Mortal).<br /> <br /> Take New York City. The latest census estimated 8,491,079 people. Let's round that to 8.5 million for convenience.<br /> <br /> This gives us:<br /> <br /> As many Mummies and Prometheans as the ST deems fit.<br /> 8 Demons?<br /> 85 Sin-Eaters (and Demons? and Beasts?).<br /> 850 Changelings and Mages.<br /> 1700 Vampires and Werewolves.<br /> 8500 Hunters and Minor Template Mortals.<br /> <br /> All of this adds up to 11143 people &quot;in the know&quot; about the supernatural, the vast majority of which have some supernatural capability of their own. This is 0.131% of New York's population. If we narrow it down to Major Templates only, the number is reduced to 2643 creatures, or 0.031%.<br /> <br /> I am personally quite happy with these numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-21-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:58:17-08:00","id":834388,"title":"","content":"Changelings are made, not born, so the ratios can vary widely, and things can happen to drop or raise the population.<br /> <br /> Vancouver has 2 Changelings, because something bad happened there for example.<br /> <br /> I think the .5% of population, with 3/4 being minor templates is good ratio for most cities that do not have something disrupting they're numbers.<br /> <br /> So in the GTA the population is 6,000,000 people, that's a Supernatural template population of 30,000, not including those with a supernatural merit.<br /> <br /> 7,500 of that is major templates. Promeathans nomadic, so I won't include them as long term inhabitants for this calculation and mummies are usually too low in population to worry about, out side of a few cities like Washington DC so I'll leave them out too. Ghosts, Hobgoblins, Spirits, Angels and thst like I don't even include in the 30,000.<br /> <br /> That leaves Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings, Sineaters, Demons, and Beasts.<br /> <br /> That's 1,070 per group, but since Changeling is the main splat for Toronto and Werewolves tend to have smaller populations, I'll say make the Changeling population 1,430 and werewolves (and Changeling Breeds) 720.<br /> <br /> This 1,430 population is divided between 3 freeholds, a with the Sultana's freehold being by far the largest and the Seasonal and Seelie freeholds being much smaller rebel Freeholds, but which have access to outside allies in other cities.<br /> <br /> So the Seasonal Freehold and Seelie Freehold could have say 200 each.<br /> <br /> That leaves 1000 for the main Freehold.<br /> <br /> Divided between the main 4 courts thats 250 each, while if the Ruby court isn't extinct anymore, then the last 30 could be members of the elitist Ruby Court.<br /> <br /> Breaking that down further, the Jade Court could have say 8 monarchs answering the Emperor of the Court, with each Monarch having roughly 25 members of their ethinic group, the rest answering directly to the Emperor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:01:55-08:00","id":834473,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834381#post834381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My eyebally rule of thumb is to have a number of tiers:<br /> <br /> Tier 0: Limited number in existence (Mummy).<br /> Tier 1: One per million (Promethean, possibly Demon and Beast?).<br /> Tier 2: One per hundred thousand (Sin-Eater, possibly Demon and Beast?).<br /> Tier 3: One per ten thousand (Changeling, Mage).<br /> Tier 4: One per five thousand (Vampire, Werewolf).<br /> Tier 5: One per thousand (Hunter, Minor Template Mortal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean's are also Tier 0 Per &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; ( I could swear I found something about 30 or 40 worldwide but I don't see it atm). given the square miles of new york if 8 prometheans lived there, the wastelands would be devastating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only a handful of the creatures walk the Earth at any given time, and some<br /> of them live their whole lives without running afoul of hunters<br /> or anyone connected to them. </div> </div> </div>I wonder if Sin-Eater should be higher? at a glance conceptually I would think that they're closer to changeling or even vampire, mediums and all that?<br /> <br /> Thing about most of the non Promethean creatures is (no comment on mummy), they're social creatures, so when you get 1 in an area more tend to follow. the 1:20000 is an average across the entire population. So for medium cities you might end up with an unusually large number or Vampires per capita, but small cities or wilderness will tend to less than that.<br /> <br /> In my mind if you have less than 10 members per &quot;Faction&quot; it's really not worth of thinking of things divided this way. So say vampires, for populations of less than 50 the clan's and covenants aren't going to seem that important (or maybe they're polarizingly blazingly imporant in a catholics vs protestants old world sort of way). But as mentioned in communities that small everyone knows everyone, so it doesn't leave much room to add throwaway NPCs. I would tend towards a higher population in most games, so that I could create throwaway NPCs of that splat type. Basically I'm saying you probably want to lean towards greater than 200 so it's reasonable that your PCs don't know everyone.<br /> <br /> I'm building my Detroit City right now, and something to keep in mind in that city, it once had a much higher population so having more than 1 monster per 20k makes sense because the people are &quot;leaving&quot; (did they leave? how many of those people are still paying taxes elsewhere... ) that the monster population might not dip, which might be why the city turned into a post apocalyptic vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 02-21-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:06:16-08:00","id":834475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834473#post834473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean's are also Tier 0 Per &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; ( I could swear I found something about 30 or 40 worldwide but I don't see it atm).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going by the implications in the Promethean corebook. Very rare, but not limited in number. At least that's what I remember, haven't checked in a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834473#post834473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Sin-Eater should be higher? at a glance conceptually I would think that they're closer to changeling or even vampire, mediums and all that?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC Sin-Eaters are rare, as there are no current Tier 3 Krewes (and Sin-Eater rarity was used as an explanation for that). Since they're still common enough to form Tier 2 Krewes (and the mechanics for Tier 3 exist), I feel comfortable with their tier placement. If I had to hazard a guess, I'd say Beasts fit that tier as well. No clue about Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:21:21-08:00","id":834483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834475#post834475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going by the implications in the Promethean corebook. Very rare, but not limited in number. At least that's what I remember, haven't checked in a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Matt's forum posts, Mortal Remains and most of the 1e supplements were written under the assumption that the global Promethean population rarely broke into the triple digits. There's definitely not an arbitrary-but-finite number of them like there are with the Arisen, particularly in 2e where the Extempore are more obviously a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:26:54-08:00","id":834487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834483#post834483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Matt's forum posts, Mortal Remains and most of the 1e supplements were written under the assumption that the global Promethean population rarely broke into the triple digits. There's definitely not an arbitrary-but-finite number of them like there are with the Arisen, particularly in 2e where the Extempore are more obviously a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. One per hundred million would give us about 70 Prometheans, give or take. I think that fits the allotted numbers and still gives me a &quot;one per&quot; measure for me to calculate on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:30:58-08:00","id":834490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834475#post834475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going by the implications in the Promethean corebook. Very rare, but not limited in number. At least that's what I remember, haven't checked in a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not limited by any known means but very very rare, I would definitely guess rarer than mummies but perhaps not *active* mummies. Big thing here though is to remember most of them are probably moving around quite frequently so you wouldn't have 8 in a city at a time, though 8 might pass through new york over the course of the year. My 2 cents largely based on that statement in Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> further reflection I think your werewolf population is probably high given their pack structure, need to roam, and genetic only lineage, I would think that vampires outnumber werewolves maybe 3:1. So could fit within the same overall populace, just not a 50/50 split, imho. it's also worth saying that I did the math, and Detroit would have had ~360 total vampires/wolves in 1950.<br /> <br /> Aha, found it, the created number less than 100 on the planet at any given time, Mortal remains p16<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Prometheans are extremely<br /> rare. Vampires, werewolves, and mages aren\u2019t<br /> especially common, but they are numerous<br /> enough to form their own organizations,<br /> secret societies, and cliques. The Created<br /> number less than 100 on the planet at any<br /> given time. Their \u201csociety\u201d consists of word<br /> of mouth, a loose form of marks left for other pilgrims (which<br /> hunters are free to find and misinterpret), and epistles sent to<br /> other Prometheans. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:40:50-08:00","id":834493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834490#post834490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">further reflection I think your werewolf population is probably high given their pack structure, need to roam, and genetic only lineage, I would think that vampires outnumber werewolves maybe 3:1. So could fit within the same overall populace, just not a 50/50 split, imho. it's also worth saying that I did the math, and Detroit would have had ~360 total vampires/wolves in 1950.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO the splits should be left up to the Storyteller. In Detroit, under your 3:1 split, would've had 90 werewolves and 270 vampires. If that sounds reasonable to you, the system works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834490#post834490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha, found it, the created number less than 100 on the planet at any given time, Mortal remains p16</div> </div> </div> </div>Yah, Satchel pointed that out to me. I've corrected my original post and taken some wild guesses on Demon and Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:52:33-08:00","id":834497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834493#post834493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO the splits should be left up to the Storyteller. In Detroit, under your 3:1 split, would've had 90 werewolves and 270 vampires. If that sounds reasonable to you, the system works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yah, Satchel pointed that out to me. I've corrected my original post and taken some wild guesses on Demon and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't disagree, that it's up to the ST. I just speculate in the city that there are more vamps than wolves, in the wilderness though... and that's another problem there might be 90 wolves *in* Detroit, that doesn't mean there's not another 45 in the spaces between the next city, Detroit is sprawling, and there's a lot of woods around it. For me I want enough vampires that you can ash vampires you don't know, with wolves I've less of a need for that (also think they're harder to kill).<br /> <br /> yeah sorry I was reading and composing a response, still having a page number is nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:23:08-08:00","id":834513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834381#post834381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My eyebally rule of thumb is to have a number of tiers:<br /> This gives us:<br /> <br /> As many Mummies and Prometheans as the ST deems fit.<br /> 8 Demons?<br /> 85 Sin-Eaters (and Beasts?).<br /> 850 Changelings and Mages.<br /> 1700 Vampires and Werewolves.<br /> 8500 Hunters and Minor Template Mortals.<br /> <br /> All of this adds up to 11143 people &quot;in the know&quot; about the supernatural, the vast majority of which have some supernatural capability of their own. This is 0.131% of New York's population. If we narrow it down to Major Templates only, the number is reduced to 2643 creatures, or 0.031%.<br /> <br /> I am personally quite happy with these numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems low for Demons, considering they have enough structure to have both &quot;rings&quot; and &quot;agencies&quot;, unless we wanted to go with global agencies... but even then... keep in mind NYC is a *huge* city population wise compared to most cities of the world (probably why it's a bad city to model against). I think they're probably in the same population pool as Sin-Eaters and Beasts, though I might think that those are 85 each, not 85 combined, and only because NYC is huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:29:54-08:00","id":834517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834513#post834513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems low for Demons, considering they have enough structure to have both &quot;rings&quot; and &quot;agencies&quot;, unless we wanted to go with global agencies... but even then... keep in mind NYC is a *huge* city population wise compared to most cities of the world (probably why it's a bad city to model against). I think they're probably in the same population pool as Sin-Eaters and Beasts, though I might think that those are 85 each, not 85 combined, and only because NYC is huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read Demon, so I have no clue whatsoever on how it works.<br /> <br /> Also, NYC is actually fairly on par with most huge cities of the world. It's not a capital, but it's on the same ballpark, population wise.<br /> <br /> That said, I'll probably edit my post again and throw demons with the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:32:58-08:00","id":834518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834513#post834513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems low for Demons, considering they have enough structure to have both &quot;rings&quot; and &quot;agencies&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agencies are an optional level of organization and a ring is literally just a small group of demons who regularly work together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:38:24-08:00","id":834522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834490#post834490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">further reflection I think your werewolf population is probably high given their pack structure, need to roam, and genetic only lineage, I would think that vampires outnumber werewolves maybe 3:1. So could fit within the same overall populace, just not a 50/50 split, imho. it's also worth saying that I did the math, and Detroit would have had ~360 total vampires/wolves in 1950.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves aren't limited by genetics. Seeing a werewolf can potentially turn you into a werewolf.<br /> <br /> While I've always been a proponent of 'Do what fits for your story,' Changeling demographics are notoriously disconnected from human demographics. It says this in a few places throughout the books, where large cities like New York have few changelings compared to small towns with dozens. This is likely due to the True Fae, who are not obliged to follow society's rules and flock to large population centers. One of the Gentry can take one life from a village every generation, while entire cities can never be touched by them. It's further reinforced by the fact that not every changeling who is taken makes it back, and not every changeling who makes it back moves back into their own life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-21-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:59:34-08:00","id":834532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834522#post834522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves aren't limited by genetics. Seeing a werewolf can potentially turn you into a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait, what? where is that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:01:18-08:00","id":834534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834518#post834518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agencies are an optional level of organization and a ring is literally just a small group of demons who regularly work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes but only 8 in all of NYC seems really low for something that has an &quot;optional&quot; level, given it's one of the largest cities. I would expect NYC to have a couple of agencies at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:04:04-08:00","id":834538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834532#post834532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, what? where is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf 2e, under dramatically failing a Lunacy roll. It makes the mortal a Wolfblooded, who can theoretically go through a First Change some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:06:26-08:00","id":834542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834532#post834532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, what? where is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Several places throughout the book, but notably in the Lunacy section and Wolf-Blooded appendix. Some people are just randomly chosen by the Moon or the Hunt, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:07:54-08:00","id":834545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834532#post834532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, what? where is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 101, the rules for Lunacy. Dramatic Failure on a Lunacy roll turns a human into a Wolf-Blooded. So, it's a bit of a stretch to say &quot;seeing a werewolf can turn you into one&quot;, but it's not technically inaccurate. If you've got enough penalties to the Breaking Point roll stacked up to put you on a chance die, you've got a 1/10 chance of becoming Wolf-Blooded, and some Wolf-Blooded go on to become Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:10:33-08:00","id":834547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834545#post834545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 101, the rules for Lunacy. Dramatic Failure on a Lunacy roll turns a human into a Wolf-Blooded. So, it's a bit of a stretch to say &quot;seeing a werewolf can turn you into one&quot;, but it's not technically inaccurate. If you've got enough penalties to the Breaking Point roll stacked up to put you on a chance die, you've got a 1/10 chance of becoming Wolf-Blooded, and some Wolf-Blooded go on to become Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that can be as high as 90%, if you consider that you can turn a failure into a dramatic failure to take a Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:14:51-08:00","id":834549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834547#post834547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that can be as high as 90%, if you consider that you can turn a failure into a dramatic failure to take a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure. A player that <i>wants</i> their character to become Wolf-Blooded can do it much more easily, but PCs are always exceptions to the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:16:37-08:00","id":834551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834549#post834549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, sure. A player that <i>wants</i> their character to become Wolf-Blooded can do it much more easily, but PCs are always exceptions to the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware there were mechanics that were restricted to PCs. I've always used full transparency between PCs and NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:19:47-08:00","id":834554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that'd put only 16 changelings for the region my group was going to be in and that region is the third most populated in the state (and since it's australia states are not small).... Can't believe someone would want even less than 1:20 000 considering how small that makes supernatural populations.<br /> <br /> edit: Wait... No 16 Major template supernaturals..... Well there goes werewolves and changelings....</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the 1:20.000 is per splat, in average, so all the 10 splats accounted for makes it 1:2.000. So, yeah, it would make for 16 changelings <u>in average</u> for a region with three hundred, twenty thousand people. And sorry but, even if it is big for your state, it isn't that big at all.<br /> <br /> Second, I presented the two numbers (1:2.000 and 1:20.000) precisely because you can play with them. Shrink a splat and you will have space for more of the others. That without stretching the supernatural population.<br /> <br /> Third, supernatural societies in the CoD <u><b>are</b></u> meant for metropolitan areas. At least as &quot;complete&quot; social structures. They aren't meant to be like this in smaller regions.<br /> <br /> Fourth, do not forget the <b>Minor</b> templates, unique supernatural creatures and generally aware humans, like blue-book PCs. You should both take into account their numbers in the region and use them in your favor. You don't need every NPC to be a &quot;pure M-Splat&quot;.<br /> <br /> Fifth, you can simply ignore all of this for your game without stretching credibility. You should only think of the consequences. A region with 320.000 people and 320 vampires have to account for the consequences of 1 bloodsucking predator for every 1.000 people. This does have consequences. The community should be affected in various ways for so much vampires. And this can be carried over to other supernaturals. Just think how they affect people around them, and extrapolate to a situation of &quot;overcrowding&quot; Changeling population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:21:46-08:00","id":834557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834551#post834551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware there were mechanics that were restricted to PCs. I've always used full transparency between PCs and NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not drawing a line between things that exist to encourage real individual humans to behave in a certain way when portraying their characters and things that happen to characters who are extensions of the setting is going to result in weird shenanigans. The average mortal NPC isn't going to &quot;choose&quot; to catastrophically fail a roll that their self-image is dependent upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:21:48-08:00","id":834558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834551#post834551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware there were mechanics that were restricted to PCs. I've always used full transparency between PCs and NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, theoretically an NPC could turn a failure into a dramatic failure for a point of Willpower (since NPCs don't accrue Beats by RAW), but... Why? The character is under STcontrol, right? If the ST wants a human NPC to become Wolf-Blooded, they don't need to wait for a failed Lunacy roll, they can just say it happened off-camera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:24:00-08:00","id":834561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834545#post834545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, it's a bit of a stretch to say &quot;seeing a werewolf can turn you into one&quot;, but it's not technically inaccurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it could 'potentially' turn you into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:25:56-08:00","id":834563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834561#post834561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said it could 'potentially' turn you into one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't disagree. Sorry if I sounded curt, that wasn't my intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:28:11-08:00","id":834567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834563#post834563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't disagree. Sorry if I sounded curt, that wasn't my intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine, I just wanted to be clear.<br /> <br /> Regarding New York and Demons, while I'm woefully behind on my Demon reading, New York seems like a place that would be bursting at the seams with Infrastructure, angels and cults of the God Machine, a particularly dangerous place for demons to hang out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:30:51-08:00","id":834570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834557#post834557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not drawing a line between things that exist to encourage real individual humans to behave in a certain way when portraying their characters and things that happen to characters who are extensions of the setting is going to result in weird shenanigans. The average mortal NPC isn't going to &quot;choose&quot; to catastrophically fail a roll that their self-image is dependent upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am forced to disagree. I think it might be interesting if an NPC mortal or Hunter keeps deliberately exposing himself to their Lunacy in order to be like them. It's creepy in that &quot;stalker fan&quot; kind of way. You can easily describe the NPC deliberately choosing to dramatically fail the Lunacy roll as &quot;embracing the madness with open arms&quot; or something equally evocative, and it will be a memorable event for the players. And even if you don't wan to go the stalker fan way, you can simply have the Integrity loss (and that exact damage to their self-image you describe) cause a Stockholm-like psychological shift on some mortals affected by Lunacy, causing them to want to be like the terrifying creatures they're witnessing. It opens interesting storytelling avenues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834558#post834558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yeah, theoretically an NPC could turn a failure into a dramatic failure for a point of Willpower (since NPCs don't accrue Beats by RAW), but... Why? The character is under STcontrol, right? If the ST wants a human NPC to become Wolf-Blooded, they don't need to wait for a failed Lunacy roll, they can just say it happened off-camera.</div> </div> </div> </div>The illusion of verisimilitude. Players are more likely to get invested and feel the setting is verisimile if they see something happening as a result of a dice roll than if it simply happens off-screen because of plot magic. Having mastery of the finer points of a setting's mechanics is much like knowing sleight of hand tricks to awe your audience in a performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:36:53-08:00","id":834575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834567#post834567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine, I just wanted to be clear.<br /> <br /> Regarding New York and Demons, while I'm woefully behind on my Demon reading, New York seems like a place that would be bursting at the seams with Infrastructure, angels and cults of the God Machine, a particularly dangerous place for demons to hang out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> at the same time demon's use aether which is GM pollution, and they need lots of desperate people to form contracts, and many of them want to attack or subborn said infrastructure. Everyone is anonymous in New York... seems like a great place for demons, but this is just nitpicking I'm simply saying 8 in a population of 8 million seems low and wouldn't really support Demons social structure as documented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:42:41-08:00","id":834577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834570#post834570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am forced to disagree. I think it might be interesting if an NPC mortal or Hunter keeps deliberately exposing himself to their Lunacy in order to be like them. It's creepy in that &quot;stalker fan&quot; kind of way. You can easily describe the NPC deliberately choosing to dramatically fail the Lunacy roll as &quot;embracing the madness with open arms&quot; or something equally evocative, and it will be a memorable event for the players. And even if you don't wan to go the stalker fan way, you can simply have the Integrity loss (and that exact damage to their self-image you describe) cause a Stockholm-like psychological shift on some mortals affected by Lunacy, causing them to want to be like the terrifying creatures they're witnessing. It opens interesting storytelling avenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It opens no avenues that are not already wide as an eight-lane highway by virtue of how being a Storyteller-controlled character works and choosing to upgrade a normal failure is not an in-character decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:44:10-08:00","id":834578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834577#post834577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It opens no avenues that are not already wide as an eight-lane highway by virtue of how being a Storyteller-controlled character works and choosing to upgrade a normal failure is not an in-character decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't really agree, but it's off-topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:07:19-08:00","id":834593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834381#post834381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My eyebally rule of thumb is to have a number of tiers:<br /> <br /> Tier 0: Limited number in existence (Mummy).<br /> Tier 1: One per hundred million (Promethean).<br /> Tier 2: One per hundred thousand (Sin-Eater, Demon?, Beast?).<br /> Tier 3: One per ten thousand (Changeling, Mage).<br /> Tier 4: One per five thousand (Vampire, Werewolf).<br /> Tier 5: One per thousand (Hunter, Minor Template Mortal).<br /> <br /> Take New York City. The latest census estimated 8,491,079 people. Let's round that to 8.5 million for convenience.<br /> <br /> This gives us:<br /> <br /> As many Mummies and Prometheans as the ST deems fit.<br /> 8 Demons?<br /> 85 Sin-Eaters (and Demons? and Beasts?).<br /> 850 Changelings and Mages.<br /> 1700 Vampires and Werewolves.<br /> 8500 Hunters and Minor Template Mortals.<br /> <br /> All of this adds up to 11143 people &quot;in the know&quot; about the supernatural, the vast majority of which have some supernatural capability of their own. This is 0.131% of New York's population. If we narrow it down to Major Templates only, the number is reduced to 2643 creatures, or 0.031%.<br /> <br /> I am personally quite happy with these numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally I'd divide most of those numbers by 10, and fill the gap with minor templates. 850 Mages, for instance, seems ridiculously high, as does nearly 2000 Vampires. 8 Demons seems right, but I'd bolster the number of stigmatics considerably. Personally I tend to favor a 1:10 or more big splat to minor version ratio, then toss in a bundle of the splats primary antagonists/plot-devices so they have something to interact with, so that'd look like:<br /> <br /> Vampires: ~200 Kindred, and ~2000 combined Ghouls, Revenants and Blood Slaves.<br /> Werewolves: ~100 Uratha, and ~3000 combined Wolf-Blooded, Spirit Touched, and weird kin.<br /> Mages: ~25 Awakened, and ~1000 combined Thaumaturges and Proximi (waaay more Thaumaturges, like 100:1)<br /> Prometheans: ~5 (possibly more since New York is a big hub and many Prommies may see it as a place to learn about humanity), and ~100 or so Alchemists, Pandorans, and other weird Principle things.<br /> Changelings: ~150 Lost, and ~500 combined Fae-Touched, Earth Bound Goblins and Fae (lots more in the hedge)<br /> Sin-Eaters: ~15 Bound (being as their fluff favors Urban Areas), and ~1000 or so psychics, ghosts and abmortals.<br /> Mummy: Maybe one or two, and ~100 or so mummy spawn and weird creatures who's names I don't currently recall. Cultist count may vary considerably.<br /> Demon: ~10 Unchained (again owing to the urban zone), and ~1000 Stigmatics and offspring (skewing stigmatic 100:1)<br /> Beasts: ~25 Begotten (once more owing to the city as a gathering point)<br /> <br /> Oh, and since everything with a supernatural ability is a Sleepwalker...somewhere around 5000 of them.<br /> <br /> So that'd come to about 500 Major Splats, and 10,000 minor splats and offspring. Which, IMO, makes a pretty huge supernatural population, even for New York. But as others have said, the real answer is however many you feel is right for your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-21-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:49:02-08:00","id":834613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834593#post834593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally I'd divide most of those numbers by 10, and fill the gap with minor templates. 850 Mages, for instance, seems ridiculously high, as does nearly 2000 Vampires. 8 Demons seems right, but I'd bolster the number of stigmatics considerably. Personally I tend to favor a 1:10 or more big splat to minor version ratio, then toss in a bundle of the splats primary antagonists/plot-devices so they have something to interact with, so that'd look like:<br /> <br /> Vampires: ~200 Kindred, and ~2000 combined Ghouls, Revenants and Blood Slaves.<br /> Werewolves: ~100 Uratha, and ~3000 combined Wolf-Blooded, Spirit Touched, and weird kin.<br /> Mages: ~25 Awakened, and ~1000 combined Thaumaturges and Proximi (waaay more Thaumaturges, like 100:1)<br /> Prometheans: ~5 (possibly more since New York is a big hub and many Prommies may see it as a place to learn about humanity), and ~100 or so Alchemists, Pandorans, and other weird Principle things.<br /> Changelings: ~50 Lost, and ~500 combined Fae-Touched, Earth Bound Goblins and Fae (lots more in the hedge)<br /> Sin-Eaters: ~15 Bound (being as their fluff favors Urban Areas), and ~1000 or so psychics, ghosts and abmortals.<br /> Mummy: Maybe one or two, and ~100 or so mummy spawn and weird creatures who's names I don't currently recall. Cultist count may vary considerably.<br /> Demon: ~10 Unchained (again owing to the urban zone), and ~1000 Stigmatics and offspring (skewing stigmatic 100:1)<br /> Beasts: ~25 Begotten (once more owing to the city as a gathering point)<br /> <br /> Oh, and since everything with a supernatural ability is a Sleepwalker...somewhere around 5000 of them.<br /> <br /> So that'd come to about 400 Major Splats, and 10,000 minor splats and offspring. Which, IMO, makes a pretty huge supernatural population, even for New York. But as others have said, the real answer is however many you feel is right for your story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering salem has about three times that many awakened and apparently that many more. I'd probably make the populations of the major ones about 200-300 larger. I feel like these numbers are a lot lower than they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:02:40-08:00","id":834616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834613#post834613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering salem has about three times that many awakened and apparently that many more. I'd probably make the populations of the major ones about 200-300 larger. I feel like these numbers are a lot lower than they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here's the thing about running large populations of Major Splats, it's fucking hard.<br /> <br /> I'll use Mage as an example: Lets say one of the PC characters gets in some trouble and has to do some big, bang-bang spell slinging to get out of it. Makes a huge supernal boom, registers on the unseen senses of all those around, you know, cool climactic stuff. Now lets say the story has ~150 Mages packed into an area like Salem, it'd be fairly reasonable to assume that maybe 10%, no let's make it 5% come to check out what happened (Mages are, after all, a nosey folk). That's 7 characters, big name NPCs with real Awakened power, with obsessions, virtues, interests, opinions and fears to work out. And it won't always be the same seven.<br /> <br /> Now the storyteller could always just handwave it, fade some or most of them into the background as irrelevant to the current story. But I'm not terribly fond of sweeping a dozen borderline demigods under the rug. And as the story and setting grows it gets harder and harder to juggle all those balls, especially if you're going for some big climax. The players will start asking things like &quot;hey, why don't we get those other 15 Arrows to come help us quash this Abyssal incursion&quot; and things like that. Even in little things players are likely to wonder about hitting up random NPCs for help and advice, dragging more and more characters into the plot. Now that's not necessarily bad, but it is difficult to manage as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> Hence I favor smaller populations, ones that I can reasonably manage without lumping 90% of them into &quot;background randos&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>There's also the character saturation problem: With 150 Mages in one area, even if that's only a small population, it will likely result in the players interacting primarily with other mages. Enough that even if it that is a small drop in the population bucket the impression will be that there are mages bloody everywhere, and they are the only characters of interest. Small populations maintains that feel that the PCs are really special, the 1% of the 1% of the 1%, which I find encourages player agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-21-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:09:20-08:00","id":834620,"title":"","content":"The key to running large populations of important characters (in any genre) is to give them something to do that's more important to them than what's happening to the players.<br /> <br /> The 65 Arrows can't come help because 30 of them are chasing down an extremely organised cabal of Banishers, 5 are consumed by their obsessions to the point where they're borderline solipsistic, 10 are hunting down a couple of Scelesti, and the other 20 are caught up in political strife, personal problems, other crises or just having a really, really shitty day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:14:55-08:00","id":834622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834620#post834620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key to running large populations of important characters (in any genre) is to give them something to do that's more important to them than what's happening to the players.<br /> <br /> The 65 Arrows can't come help because 30 of them are chasing down an extremely organised cabal of Banishers, 5 are consumed by their obsessions to the point where they're borderline solipsistic, 10 are hunting down a couple of Scelesti, and the other 20 are caught up in political strife, personal problems, other crises or just having a really, really shitty day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, right. But it's still more to juggle, and a constant consideration in the storyteller's mind. Not to mention a really great way for the players to get derailed attempting to knock down the Doors (e.g. social maneuvering) of those Banisher hunters, or hit up their Contacts contacts, or jumping onto that Scelesti hunt (because when a storyteller mentions something like that most players tend to take it as a plot hook to pursue. Mine would). And that's a viable way to play, but not one I'm particularly fond of.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Really though this is a problem that only arises when you explicitly set out population numbers. As others have said, the proper way to handle populations is &quot;however many is right for my story&quot;. That gives the storyteller the most narrative control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-21-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:29:42-08:00","id":834662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834554#post834554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sorry but, even if it is big for your state, it isn't that big at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third, supernatural societies in the CoD <u><b>are</b></u> meant for metropolitan areas. At least as &quot;complete&quot; social structures. They aren't meant to be like this in smaller regions. </div> </div> </div>The issue is that it is big for australia. It's one of the most populated regions on the continent. Your number seems to only work in the most populated of the most populated places on the planet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth, do not forget the <b>Minor</b> templates, unique supernatural creatures and generally aware humans, like blue-book PCs. You should both take into account their numbers in the region and use them in your favor. You don't need every NPC to be a &quot;pure M-Splat&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes? I'm not sure why you stated this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T16:22:13-08:00","id":834683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834616#post834616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's the thing about running large populations of Major Splats, it's fucking hard.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>There's also the character saturation problem: With 150 Mages in one area, even if that's only a small population, it will likely result in the players interacting primarily with other mages. Enough that even if it that is a small drop in the population bucket the impression will be that there are mages bloody everywhere, and they are the only characters of interest. Small populations maintains that feel that the PCs are really special, the 1% of the 1% of the 1%, which I find encourages player agency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me and my group, this is a positive thing. Our CofD games don't mix splats, to the point that we have a recurring charactre, Sgt, Moreta, who is in all games but its never the same guy. For all intents are purposes there are only mortals, changelings and their derivatives in the city, maybe some mortal thaumaturges, but nothin more than that.<br /> <br /> I want a rich population of changeling to allow a wide range of interaction and npcs. I want to have more that one freehold were no one really nows everyone, or most changelings. I want to evoke the feeling of a diaspora, living within the city, they are a large number of &quot;expats&quot; with more in common than most, living as a small nation within the city.<br /> <br /> I generally look for uniqueness in games of mages, vampire or werewolf. And even find it imposible for a city to have too many of those splats without serious consequences. But i don't feel that changelings really pose that problem. I can't really find a problem with a large population of changelings in the city, yes it might change the flavor of the game, but i can't find a problem with.<br /> <br /> I can plausibly see a large city with 5% of its population being changelings without much problems, even if im not really aiming at such high proportions. Actually when you get to such numbers, i think the intensity fae presence in the city is more problematic for mortals than the changeling themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","user":"Quimeradc","date":". 02-21-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T16:27:28-08:00","id":834688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834683#post834683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me and my group, this is a positive thing. Our CofD games don't mix splats, to the point that we have a recurring charactre, Sgt, Moreta, who is in all games but its never the same guy. For all intents are purposes there are only mortals, changelings and their derivatives in the city, maybe some mortal thaumaturges, but nothin more than that.<br /> <br /> I want a rich population of changeling to allow a wide range of interaction and npcs. I want to have more that one freehold were no one really nows everyone, or mot changelings. I want to evoke the feeling of a diaspora, or the living within the city, they are a large number of &quot;expats&quot; with more in common than most, living as a small nation within the city.<br /> <br /> I generally look for uniqueness in games of mages, vampire or werewolf. And even find it imposible for a city to have too many of those splats without serious consequences. But i don't feel that changelings really pose that problem. I can't really find a problem with a large population of changelings in the city, yes it might change the flavor of the game, but i can't find a problem with.<br /> <br /> I can plausibly see a large city with 5% of its population being changelings without much problems, even if im not really aiming at such high proportions. Actually when you get to such numbers, i think the intensity fae presence in the city is more problematic for mortals than the changeling themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'll agree with you on the Changeling front. Changeling stories are exceptionally personal, and the 2e additions of approaches and the changes to courts does a wonderful job of keeping a Changeling's problems their own. Actually, the meta-story angle of Changeling is probably what does it. In a Vampire game there's really no reason not to go poking around for NPCs, in Changeling is a serious risk to you and them. Because if they help out, now their caught up in your fucking story, and they know this.<br /> <br /> Man I love Changeling...<br /> <br /> Anyway, those populations are absolutely biased by my favoring crossover and minispats. I'd probably kick up the Changeling numbers in a non-crossover game. In fact, I'll kick them up right now. *goes to edit post*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T17:27:34-08:00","id":834713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834373#post834373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok thanks for all the answers so far. A few extra things to consider. Firstly my groups worlds of darkness differ particualry from the standard game in that there are no other splats in the games. For all intents and purposes, tehre are onyl mortals, changelings and their antagonists in a city. That i believe can extend the number of since changelings are relatively harmless to humans. Yes there would be a lot of abductions but fetches take care of many of those and not all changelings coming back most have being taken from the same city. And depresion or stress could be a reasonable explanation for few thousand reticent mortals in a city<br /> <br /> And for the purposes of this topic a want to go large. whats stopping me from having a 1:1000 ratio of changelings in a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real thing isn't the exact number, just how this affects your city. First, it means a lot of abductions, or a reason for this place to attract so many Changelings on their escapes. Second, it means so many fae in a city that the average citizen will find some every day just in the way to work, even if never realizing it or having any consequence. Just think about how much people you see in the streets every day just for walking half an hour. Third, it does means a lot of strange phenomena happening regularly, and most people are touched by the fae in their lives, if not almost all of them. 1:1.000 is enough for Changelings to be a force in the city without any power whatsoever. They are simply that great a minority.<br /> <br /> You probably don't need such numbers as much as you think, but actually nothing stops you from making a city where the Changeling ratio is 1:20. At most I would say that at larger ratio it would be impossible for the Changelings to actually hide from the common population, so you could consider the population as typically aware of the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T22:50:28-08:00","id":834855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834616#post834616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's the thing about running large populations of Major Splats, it's fucking hard.<br /> <br /> I'll use Mage as an example: Lets say one of the PC characters gets in some trouble and has to do some big, bang-bang spell slinging to get out of it. Makes a huge supernal boom, registers on the unseen senses of all those around, you know, cool climactic stuff. Now lets say the story has ~150 Mages packed into an area like Salem, it'd be fairly reasonable to assume that maybe 10%, no let's make it 5% come to check out what happened (Mages are, after all, a nosey folk). That's 7 characters, big name NPCs with real Awakened power, with obsessions, virtues, interests, opinions and fears to work out. And it won't always be the same seven.<br /> <br /> Now the storyteller could always just handwave it, fade some or most of them into the background as irrelevant to the current story. But I'm not terribly fond of sweeping a dozen borderline demigods under the rug. And as the story and setting grows it gets harder and harder to juggle all those balls, especially if you're going for some big climax. The players will start asking things like &quot;hey, why don't we get those other 15 Arrows to come help us quash this Abyssal incursion&quot; and things like that. Even in little things players are likely to wonder about hitting up random NPCs for help and advice, dragging more and more characters into the plot. Now that's not necessarily bad, but it is difficult to manage as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> Hence I favor smaller populations, ones that I can reasonably manage without lumping 90% of them into &quot;background randos&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>There's also the character saturation problem: With 150 Mages in one area, even if that's only a small population, it will likely result in the players interacting primarily with other mages. Enough that even if it that is a small drop in the population bucket the impression will be that there are mages bloody everywhere, and they are the only characters of interest. Small populations maintains that feel that the PCs are really special, the 1% of the 1% of the 1%, which I find encourages player agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand to a certain extent but I feel like a few hundred people spread over 8 million people. Should be at bear minimum 800 with a 1:1000 ratio. That city has 8 million people. With shit going on everywhere. If it only had 25 mages. That would mean there's literally no mages in the world and at best 10k. Salem having 150 I'd consider abnormal but it's a historically magic town. However, the point is the numbers across the board should be a lot larger. If it were a small town I could see the numbers presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T23:12:54-08:00","id":834860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834254-changeling-the-lost-demographic?p=834855#post834855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand to a certain extent but I feel like a few hundred people spread over 8 million people. Should be at bear minimum 800 with a 1:1000 ratio. That city has 8 million people. With shit going on everywhere. If it only had 25 mages. That would mean there's literally no mages in the world and at best 10k. Salem having 150 I'd consider abnormal but it's a historically magic town. However, the point is the numbers across the board should be a lot larger. If it were a small town I could see the numbers presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree, I might have gone overboard (underboard?) with the numbers, but 800 is IMO a ridiculous, unmanagable number. If this were Ascension I'd give it the nod, but in Awakening it'd be a hell of a thing to run.<br /> <br /> I think all-in-all the X:Y population comparison is flawed, it assumes that the splats congregate based on averages. In most cases this is simply not true, Vampires tend to favor metropolitan areas and Werewolf definitely prefer rural ones. Mages, at least how I tend to run them, probably don't like too many others crowding in on their research, and 800 mages in one relatively tight area is super fucking crowded. To stay on topic Changelings are the polar opposite, they benefit from having a bunch of other Changelings around and therefore are likely to congregate heavily in storied places like NYC.<br /> <br /> But as I said in my last post, the best solution is not to define populations at all. They adapt to the story <b>you </b>want to tell, and even the SAS's and city write ups should merely be taken as inspirational material, and not hard canon (CofD shys away from that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-22-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:59:57-08:00","id":834973,"title":"","content":"Upper Michigan has 311,361 people and the sample freehold from the CC section is an example of a rural setting. We only know a bit about it, but it has 4 courts with the 1:20,000 figure giving them roughly 16 'native' changelings. That may not be too far off, maybe a few more changelings from Wisconsin or lower Michigan bringing the freehold's numbers up to 20ish. Going by the '10th dots of mantle' to keep a court stable and 4-5 changelings in a court means things are probably pretty precarious and the freehold is holding in by the skin of it's teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:08:29-08:00","id":835251,"title":"","content":"The needs of the Freehold's functionality should trump the 1:20,000 rule or rules like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T13:12:21-08:00","id":835308,"title":"","content":"Of course it all depends of what you need and want for your chronicle, that goes without saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}